; claude: the boards kit: a board game's rules where both the game and
; the program that trains a network to play it can reach them --
; Connect4 (the rules, what a position is worth, the hints a search is
; given, and the position as a network reads it) and Go9 (Go on 9 by
; 9: the rules, the counting, the random playout, the position as a
; network reads it and the board's eight symmetries) and Chess (the
; rules, alpha-beta with its ordering and quiescence, the position and
; a move as a network reads them). Used by AiConnect4, AiGo and
; AiChess, and by scripts/train/train_connect4, train_go and
; train_chess. No drawing: it is on the libraries
; only. In the package elm_playground_gamekits, as
; elm_playground_gamekits.kit_boards.
(library
 (name kit_boards)
 (public_name elm_playground_gamekits.kit_boards)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries elm_core ai_search ai_selfplay
  random ; claude: Lehmer, Go9's playouts
 )
)
